  <ul>
    <li>Is embraced by the Obama Administration, the National Governor's Association, the Governor's Office, Illinois P-20 Council, numerous advocacy groups and matches the goals of the Illinois Public Agenda for College and Career Success.</li>
    <li>US ranks <span data-field="rank">{{ rank }}</span> in degree attainment among G-20 countries for ages <span data-field="age_range">{{ age_range }}</span>.</li>
    <li><span data-field="job_requirement_percentage">{{ job_requirement_percentage }}</span> of jobs in Illinois will require post secondary training by <span data-field="target_year">{{ target_year }}</span>.</li>
    <li><span data-field="current_credential_percentage">{{ current_credential_percentage }}</span> of working age adults in Illinois currently hold a post secondary credential.</li>
    <li>The Illinois goal is <span data-field="goal_percentage">{{ goal_percentage }}</span> of working age adults holding post-secondary credentials by <span data-field="goal_year">{{ goal_year }}</span>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 50px;">Sources: Complete College America <a href="http://www.completecollege.org/docs/illinois.pdf">http://www.completecollege.org/docs/illinois.pdf</a> / Georgetown Center on Education and the Workforce <a href="http://cew.georgetown.edu/jobs2018/">http://cew.georgetown.edu/jobs2018/</a></p>
