<div class="page">
  <h2 style="font-size: 24pt; margin-bottom: 40px;">Methods</h2>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 30px; font-size: 12pt;">
    <li>Research Question #1: Multinomial Logistic Regression
      <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 5px;">
        <li>Used with a categorical outcome (dependent).</li>
        <li>Provides an estimate of the treatment effect (odds ratios) on each outcome category after adjusting for the other explanatory variables.</li>
        <li>Outcome of reference was not being enrolled during the study period.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Research Question #2: Survival Analysis (Cox Regression)
      <ul style="list-style-type: circle; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 5px;">
        <li>Traditionally used in medical and epidemiology research.</li>
        <li>Used to explore the relationship between a set of explanatory variables and a time-based event of interest (number of semesters until bachelor's completion).</li>
        <li>Provides an estimate of the treatment effect (odds ratios) on survival.</li>
      </ul>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

